# Decaying Soil: "Threshold -- As long as there are seven or more cards in your graveyard, this enchantment has 'Whenever a
# nontoken creature is put into your graveyard from the battlefield, you may pay {1}...'". A creature leaving the
# battlefield is looked back on (CR 603.10a): the graveyard is counted as it was before the creature arrived, so the
# creature that makes the seventh card does not trigger it.
#
# T1 Bot1 casts the Soil (the Moxen pay). T3 upkeep: nothing is in the graveyard, so the Soil's upkeep trigger exiles
# nothing and asks nothing. Bot1 casts an Ornithopter, then Brain Freeze on itself with storm 1 (one spell before it):
# two mills of three, and with Brain Freeze itself, seven cards. T5 upkeep: the Soil exiles one (the Brain Freeze, chosen from seven), so
# six remain. Bot1 casts a Walking Ballista with X = 0, which dies at once as it enters: six cards before, so no trigger
# (a check that the stack is empty), seven after. T6: Bot2's Bolt kills the Ornithopter with seven cards in the
# graveyard before it: the trigger goes on the stack, Bot1 pays {1}, and the Ornithopter returns to its hand.

